7. NUMERICAL VERIFICATION FRAMEWORK
-----------------------------------

The project defines the following verification quantities:

    Mesh convergence
    Element quality / Jacobian quality
    Inverted or degenerate element detection
    Nonlinear residual convergence
    Energy consistency
    Geometric volume preservation
    Pressure-response consistency
    Gravity-response reproducibility
    Sensitivity to fiber orientation
    Sensitivity to material parameters
    Sensitivity to basal boundary conditions
    Sensitivity to cavity pressure

Documented acceptance criteria include:

    Geometric volume divergence:
        Delta V (%) = |V_mask - V_mesh| / V_mask × 100

    Target:
        Delta V <= 1.5%

    Minimum Jacobian-quality threshold:
        > 0.35

    Nonlinear residual:
        normalized residual below the predefined solver tolerance

A strict target tolerance of 1e-5 was specified during the verification design.
The actual tolerance used for a specific execution must be confirmed from the
native COMSOL model or solver record.

