11. REPRODUCIBILITY PRINCIPLE
-----------------------------

The repository is designed to preserve reproducibility without redistributing
the underlying source imaging datasets.

Source datasets remain subject to their original access and redistribution
conditions.

Only de-identified study records, derived computational artifacts, model
documentation, parameter specifications, execution registries, and verified
results should be placed in the public repository.

12. MANUSCRIPT RECONCILIATION RULE
----------------------------------

No manuscript-facing numerical result should be treated as a final measured
COMSOL result solely because it appears in a planning table, example output,
draft solver log, illustrative CSV, or expected-result registry.

Final numerical values must be reconciled against the verified computational
source of truth.

The reconciliation hierarchy is:

    Native COMSOL *.mph model
            ↓
    Native solver / execution records
            ↓
    Patient-specific geometry and mesh artifacts
            ↓
    Raw patient × gravity exports
            ↓
    Derived numerical summaries
            ↓
    Manuscript tables
            ↓
    Manuscript figures
            ↓
    Results and Discussion text

